course: dictionary
lesson: 5401
title: Korean: a place, a people, a language
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Korean is a word that can work in three ways. It can describe something: «Korean food» is food from Korea. It can name a person: a Korean is someone from Korea or with Korean family roots. It can also name a language: Korean is what people speak in Korea.
explain: The words around it show you which one you need. «South Korea's capital is Seoul» tells you Korean is part of a country's name. «Koreans» with an s means more than one person. Always check the clues in the sentence first.
explain: Korea is a peninsula in East Asia, divided into two countries: South Korea and North Korea. Korean always starts with a capital letter, because it names a place, a people and a language.
fact: Korean means from or about Korea.
fact: A Korean is a person from Korea or with Korean family roots.
fact: Korean is also the language spoken in Korea, written with an alphabet called Hangul.
fact: «South Korea's capital is Seoul» and «North Korea's is Pyongyang».
fact: Korea has been divided since 1945, and the Korean War of 1950 to 1953 ended only in an armistice, not a peace treaty.
exercise: In the phrase «Korean food», what kind of word is Korean? | A noun for a person | *An adjective, describing the food | A verb | A full stop
exercise: Mina says, «A Korean is someone from Korea.» What is a Korean? | *A person from Korea or with Korean family roots | A language | A festival | A dish of rice and vegetables
exercise: Which alphabet is used to write Korean? | Cyrillic | Arabic | Latin | *Hangul
test: «South Korea's capital is Seoul.» What is the capital of South Korea? | Busan | *Seoul | Tokyo | Pyongyang
test: «She speaks Korean at home.» In this sentence, what is Korean? | *A language | A person | A place | A festival
exam: «Many people in Australia have Korean families.» Which noun does Korean describe here? | People | Australia | *Families | Many
